  {
   "type": "textmedia",
   "header": "<h2> Tool Management Software as a Central Component of Tool Management </h2>",
   "body": "<p>Modern tool logistics is actually unthinkable without the management software that corresponds to its needs. With the right program, you can ensure that tools are available for every work step, and the time-consuming search for tools is a thing of the past. That’s because your tool list will then also indicate where each individual part is located—and if you wish, you can use Smart Cabinets, intelligent storage cabinets, to ensure that everything is truly in its place.</p> <h3>Tool Data Always Ready</h3> <p>But tool management is much more than just tool storage: The system always has the appropriate tool data or tool presets available and enables fast, error-free transmission to your tooling systems or presetting device. This prevents errors, reduces scrap, and speeds up work processes.</p> <p>Whether you’re using cutting tools (we usually refer to them as “machining tools,” but if “cutting tools” is better from an SEO perspective, you can use that term as well) or devices from an entirely different tool class: There is certainly still room for improvement in your logistics—are there possible options for optimization, perhaps in tool dispensing, the storage system, or the tool database you use for usage?</p>",
   "images": [
